---
/** The answer, as the reference's quote: one large serif line, one word marked in lime. */
---

<section class="pc-section pc-cover quote">
  <div class="pc-wrap pc-pad body">
    <p class="pc-serif line" data-reveal>
      Forests don't need more monitoring. They need <mark>management</mark>.
    </p>
    <p class="pc-lead by">AboveForest is the operating system that makes it possible.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .quote {
    background:
      radial-gradient(60% 60% at 50% 100%, rgb(184 242 122 / 0.08), transparent 70%),
      var(--pc-dark);
  }

  .body {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 28px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .line {
    max-width: 18ch;
    font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 76px);
    line-height: 1.04;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  mark {
    padding: 0 0.12em;
    border-radius: 0.12em;
    background: var(--pc-lime);
    color: var(--pc-lime-ink);
    box-decoration-break: clone;
    -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone;
  }

  /* Inside the mark, the reveal flashes deep green instead of lime on lime. */
  mark {
    --reveal: #2f6b12;
  }

  .by {
    max-width: 34ch;
  }
</style>
